On 4 Oct 2004 12:56:41 -0700, dfreybur@yahoo.com (Doug Freyburger) wrote:


>> I know that potions of gain ability increase natural stats even with 
>> magical items, but it is hard to test stats exercising in wizmode. :)

Potion of Gain ability modify the basic attribute before modifiers are
applied.  The modifiers done by armor and the like add the +1/-1 modifiers
together (or whatever they would be) and report that the current attribute
is at the currently displayed value. 

Texting stats exercising isn't possible in Wizmode because of the number of
factors.  It's better to check the source manually - it may be hard to read
if you don't know the language, but you shouldn't have too much problem
noticing where they get exercised/abused.

>Execising stats is a separate topic from wearing magical items.

True, but there are some magical items can cause forms of exercising/abuse.
(It's indirect by granting a negative intrinsic, but it is caused by the
items.)

